course: dictionary
lesson: 8163
title: Reset: starting again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To reset something means to set it back to how it started. «Ben in Austin pressed the reset button every time he was losing a video game with his friend Luis.» Ben wanted the game to start again from the beginning, so reset means to set it back to its starting point.
explain: Reset can also mean to set something again or change it. «After a power cut, oven and microwave clocks often reset.» The clock goes back to its starting setting, so the time is wrong until someone fixes it. Reset can be a verb (to reset) or a noun (a reset).
explain: A reset can also be a fresh start. «Sleep is when your mood resets.» Your mood starts again with a clearer feeling. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Reset means to set a machine, device or counter back to its starting state.
fact: To reset a password, clock or alarm means to set it again or change it.
fact: To reset a broken bone means to put it back in the right place.
fact: As a noun, a reset is a fresh start, as in «a calm break can be a reset».
fact: Common phrases include «reset to zero», «reset the password», «press reset» and «factory reset».
exercise: «Ben pressed the reset button every time he was losing a video game.» What does reset mean here? | Make the game louder | Turn the game into a film | Hide the game for ever | *Set the game back to its starting point
exercise: A doctor resets a broken bone. What does reset mean here? | *Puts the bone back in the right place | Snaps the bone in two | Covers the bone with a bandage | Measures the bone's length
exercise: «Sleep is when your mood resets.» What does reset suggest? | A long walk in the rain | A loud noise | A sudden sad ending | *A fresh start
test: Mia forgot her password, so she had to reset it. What does reset mean here? | Say it out loud to her friend | Forget it for ever | Write it on the wall | *Set it again with a new one
test: «After a power cut, the oven clock often reset.» What happened to the clock? | It moved to another house | It stopped working for ever | *It went back to its starting setting | It got faster and faster
exam: In «a calm break can be a reset», what does reset mean? | A long walk | A loud noise | A broken machine | *A fresh start
